      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T09:32:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Abe, based on Ting Shen\u0027s suggestion(#74), a retry mechanism has been added.\n\"The registers should only be updated if they were written successfully.\"",
      "parentUuid": "26f5a402_73b77b95",
      "revId": "51929efdb157fba983e6e21064e9ce4572c82069",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef1fa538_0d2aabff",
        "filename": "zephyr/program/skywalker/yoda/src/charger.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 85,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-01T16:57:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. I\u0027m not disputing that you should check for errors on write. I\u0027m saying that unless you have any reason to believe that behavior might be different on retry, there\u0027s no reason to retry. If it fails, just return without setting `pre_battery_cells`.\n2. The way this is written now, after the retry count is exhausted, it will fall through to set `pre_battery_cells` anyway and reset `set_reg_err_count`. So if multiple retried _did_ fail every time, in would eventually become inconsistent, and it wouldn\u0027t actually stop trying.",
      "parentUuid": "79ba512d_ec38a644",
      "revId": "51929efdb157fba983e6e21064e9ce4572c82069",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
